                <pb facs="1019" n="925" xml:id="pg925"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Terrell to Mr.
                            Olney.</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Constantinople</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1896-11-25"><hi rendition="#italic">November 25,
                        1896</hi>.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p>Telegram from Harpoot that twenty-six wives with children of naturalized
                    Americans, for whom I applied to the Sultan, will leave there at once for
                    America under escort of my cavas to the seashore, and that twenty-three more
                    such women and naturalized Americans not yet ready will leave in a few days.
                    Also a telegram from Marash that the governor there facilitates departure of all
                    persons applied for by me. Until now the governor of Harpoot has obstructed the
                    orders of the Porte.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Terrell.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
